-- title:
--   Iwasawa unfolding of the unipotent cusp-kernel term
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields, $\alpha,\beta$ real numbers, $\nu_{Z_L}$ a Haar measure on the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ for a Borel structure on it, and $\Omega_L$ a fundamental domain for the subgroup of principal ideles (the range of $L^\times\to(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$) with respect to $\nu_{Z_L}$. Let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$, i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the continuous ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ compatible with the embedding of $L$; let $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau$ lies in the group generated by $\sigma$; and let $\xi_L$ be a homomorphism from the full idele group to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ whose associated complex-valued function is continuous and which is trivial on principal ideles. Let $c>0$ and $u,d_1,d_2$ be real, $T_c\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ compact, and $\Phi_0\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ a set contained in the union of the right translates by elements of $T_c$ of the centre-cut Siegel set with parameters $c,u,d_1,d_2$ (integral finite part, local height at least $c$ and window square at most $u^2$ at every infinite place, archimedean determinant norms in $[d_1,d_2]$), contained in the shell $\{g:\|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}_L}\in[\alpha,\beta]\}$, and a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with respect to the adelic Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ restricted to that shell. Let $X$ be an additive fundamental domain for $L$ in $\mathbb{A}_L$ for the adelic additive Haar measure, and $\Omega_1,\Omega_2$ fundamental domains for the principal ideles in $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ for the idelic Haar measure. Then there is a constant $\kappa\in[0,\infty]$, neither $0$ nor $\infty$, with the following property. Let $\varphi:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)\to\mathbb{C}$ be continuous with compact support and let $\mathrm{reps}\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be a cusp transversal, i.e. every $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ admits a unique $\rho\in\mathrm{reps}$ with $g\rho^{-1}$ in the Borel subgroup (lower-left entry zero). Assume that for all sufficiently large $R$ the iterated lower integral over $x\in\Phi_0$ of $\sum_{\rho}\int^-_{\Omega_L}\|\xi_L(z)(\,\mathrm{cuspKernel}-\mathrm{cuspTruncation}\,)(z,\rho x)\|$ is finite, where `TwistedBruhat.cuspKernel` sums $\varphi(g^{-1}\,\beta\,\sigma_D(z g))$ over $\beta$ in the intersection of the norm-unipotent set with the Borel subgroup and `TwistedBruhat.cuspTruncation` is the indicator of the high set $\{\mathrm{adelicHeight}>e^{R}\}$ times the constant term along the unipotent $t\mapsto\begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, taken with respect to the conditional adelic Haar measure on the adelic box, of $y\mapsto\sum_\delta\varphi(g^{-1}\delta\,\sigma_D(y))$ over the norm-one Borel set $\{\delta:\delta_{10}=0,\ N_{L/K}(\delta_{00}/\delta_{11})=1\}$, evaluated at $zg$. Then for all sufficiently large $R$ the function sending $x$ to $\int_{\Omega_L}\xi_L(z)\bigl(\sum_{\delta}\varphi(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma_D(zx))-\mathrm{cuspTruncation}(z,x)\bigr)\,d\nu_{Z_L}$, the first sum being over those $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy class has norm class equal to the conjugacy class of some $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ of unipotent type (non-central with characteristic polynomial $(X-a)^2$), is integrable on $\Phi_0$ for the adelic Haar measure, and its integral over $\Phi_0$ equals $\kappa$ (as a real number, viewed in $\mathbb{C}$) times the iterated integral over $x\in X$, $u\in\Omega_1$, $t\in\Omega_2$ and $k$ over the adelic maximal compact subgroup, with respect to the additive adelic Haar, idelic Haar, idelic Haar and the maximal-compact Haar measure, of the shell indicator of $g\mapsto\int_{\Omega_L}\xi_L(z)(\mathrm{cuspKernel}-\mathrm{cuspTruncation})(z,g)\,d\nu_{Z_L}$ evaluated at $\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}\,zI\,\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\,k$, multiplied by $\|t\|_{\mathbb{A}_L}^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the unfolding step that rewrites the unipotent-type contribution to the twisted cusp kernel, minus its truncated constant term, as an integral in Iwasawa coordinates $n\,z\,\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\,k$ with the modulus factor $\|t\|^{-1}$, the constant $\kappa$ recording the comparison of the Haar measures. It feeds the version of the same identity carrying semi-local factorisation hypotheses on the test function.
